Algorithm provenance
====================

The Ed25519 implementation in this package is an original, pure-Racket
implementation of the algorithm specified in RFC 8032 ("Edwards-Curve
Digital Signature Algorithm (EdDSA)"), section 5.1:

  - Point arithmetic uses the complete unified extended-coordinate
    addition formulas published in RFC 8032 section 5.1.4
    (Hisil-Wong-Carter-Dawson, a = -1).
  - Public-key recovery from encodings uses the decompression technique
    of the public-domain Ed25519 reference implementation "ref10"
    (Daniel J. Bernstein et al., https://ed25519.cr.yp.to/).
  - SHA-512 is implemented per FIPS 180-4; its round constants and
    initial values follow sections 4.2.3 and 5.3.3 (fractional parts of
    cube and square roots of the first primes).
  - The group order and curve constants are derived in code from the
    parameters in RFC 8032 section 5.1 rather than transcribed.

No code was copied from TweetNaCl or ref10; their published behavior is
what this implementation is validated against:

  - All RFC 8032 section 7.1 test vectors pass byte-for-byte.
  - A 1000+-case randomized cross-validation against OpenSSL 3
    (pkeyutl -rawin) confirms byte-identical signatures and mutual
    verification (tests/cross-check.rkt).
